> Interpretation and limits

Exact refers to complete tuple enumeration with floating arithmetic, not exact
real arithmetic. Sampled tuples repeat indices within a tuple and can repeat
entire tuples across draws. The callback runs once per actual term; captures are
prefixes from the same loop. Finite-value and output/work checks prevent silent
invalid results. Bias/asymptotic statements require kernel/distribution
assumptions; the variance identity is derived without a universal bias claim.

All programs are complete editable C++ sources; figures are local files. Actual
traces and selected counts come from the producing native kernels, not an
independent report reconstruction.

> References

The empirical-distribution expectation and variance-kernel U/V identity are
derived above. No unqualified asymptotic theorem is asserted.

